From 4151872f530a8964518500573a982b744cba6493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:43:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 73/73] Tangelo is licensed under GPLv3 or any later version, like Azahar

Patch 0068 brought in Azahar code that is licensed GPLv3-or-later since
Azahar's relicence, which makes Tangelo as a whole GPLv3-or-later. This
follows Azahar's own switch (upstream 86a9f92, 0ab6399, 811f690, 6280521):

- LICENSE.txt: the GPLv3 text plus the icon licences (from dist/license.md, which goes), replacing license.txt;
- misc/licenses/gplv2.txt: the GPLv2 text. Files that were "GPLv2 or any later version" stay so and now refer to it;
- Tangelo's own files (Copyright Tangelo Emulator Project) are GPLv3 or any later version, as new files are upstream (.ci/license-header.rb);
- the about dialog, the Android app description and the Windows installer's license page name GPLv3 / LICENSE.txt;
- thread_queue_list.h gets back its PPSSPP copyright line (upstream 811f690).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
